      "finding": null,
      "explanation": "The skill's description states it operates on PDF files, but this script attempts to process input as an image file. When a PDF file (the expected input per the skill description) is provided, PIL fails to parse it as a valid image, causing an unhandled exception that crashes the skill. This creates a denial-of-service vulnerability where an attacker can disrupt the skill by simply providing a legitimate PDF file input.",
      "remediation": "The skill must convert PDF pages to images before invoking this script. Specifically: (1) Use a PDF rendering library (e.g., PyMuPDF, pdf2image) to convert the target PDF page to a temporary image file (e.g., PNG), (2) Pass this temporary image as the `input_path` to the script, (3) If the validation image output is needed, return it after processing or further convert it back to PDF context if required by the workflow. Input path validation should also be added to prevent path traversal attacks.",
